BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tara McGowan & The Art of Japanese Paper Theatre
DTSTART:20261120T190000
DTEND:20261120T210000
DTSTAMP:20261120T190958Z
UID:572de6581df9123b9cddf90246ccfb@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Upstream Classical presents storyteller Tara McGowan sharing s
 tories from around the world in a one-hour show designed for all ages. Wor
 king in the Kamishibai tradition\, a century-old form of Japanese street t
 heatre that uses illustrated paper pages to accompany the tales\, McGowan 
 appears regularly at festivals across the globe including most recently in
  Mexico\, France and Slovenia. Friday’s show in Lyndon roughly coincides
  with the Japanese Festival of the Moon and a celebration of harvest time
 \, represented in this program that weaves together themes of nature\, the
  moon and the forest with magical elements. McGowan will be joined by Donn
 a Nicol on quartz crystal singing bowls and Rachael Elliott on woodwinds a
 nd percussion\, who together create acoustic soundscapes to accompany the 
 stories. Enjoy the magic of live storytelling complemented by blissful har
 monic resonances as stories and sounds merge. Tara McGowan\, storyteller D
 onna Nicol\, quartz crystal singing bowls and percussion Rachael Elliott\,
  woodwinds and percussion\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:York Street Meeting House\, 153 York St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/tara-mcgow
 an-the-art-of-japanese-paper-theatre-11-11-2026-08-59-48
END:VEVENT
