DESCRIPTION:The 25th Annual Pack the Pantry Food and Funds Drive\, present
 ed by Preston's Kia\, Chrysler\, Dodge\, Jeep and Ram. Volunteers will col
 lect canned goods\, nonperishable food and monetary gifts with the goal of
  filling a 53-foot Bellavance Trucking tractor-trailer for The Salvation A
 rmy Emergency Food Shelf. Santa visits Friday evening\; the 802 Ghostbuste
 rs and 501st Legion stormtroopers appear Saturday. Every $1 given through 
 the Red Kettle helps provide $7 worth of food\, and every gift stays local
 . Collection kits and online giving at www.vtpackthepantry.com. Market 32 
 by Price Chopper\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/25th-annua
 l-pack-the-pantry-food-and-funds-drive-22-10-2026-12-33-11
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Big Brothers Big Sisters x Barbarian Stowe Fundraiser
DTSTART:20261121T073000
DTEND:20261121T210000
DTSTAMP:20261120T190958Z
UID:f8612a2b070a98ad355e9806281730@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Give an Extra Gift This Holiday Season! Take a break from holi
 day shopping and enjoy a delicious meal at Barbarian Restaurant\, 454 Moun
 tain Rd. in Stowe\, on Saturday\, November 21. Your meal can do more than 
 satisfy your appetite\, it can help give Vermont youth the gift of a carin
 g mentor! A portion of the day's sales will support Big Brothers Big Siste
 rs of NH & VT and our youth mentoring programs. At Big Brothers Big Sister
 s\, we believe every young person deserves someone in their corner\, a car
 ing\, consistent mentor who listens\, encourages\, and helps them see what
 's possible. We build meaningful relationships between youth and trained v
 olunteer mentors that create lasting impact and help change lives for gene
 rations. Dine with us. Make a difference. Give the gift of mentorship!\n\n
 Sources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Barbarian Resturant\, 454 Mountain Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/big-brothe
 rs-big-sisters-x-barbarian-stowe-fundraiser-03-11-2026-16-44-26
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Signing for Inland Sea Author Sam Clark
DTSTART:20261121T130000
DTEND:20261121T150000
DTSTAMP:20261120T190958Z
UID:13d46b84d1d4504c77cc1a96532d43@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Plainfield author Sam Clark will sign copies of his new myster
 y Lock 9\, published by Onion River Press\, on Saturday\, Nov. 21\, from 1
 –3 p.m. at Bear Pond Books in Stowe. The sequel to The Inland Sea\, the 
 novel follows a retired Vermont State Police detective through a case of m
 istaken identity spanning Lake Champlain\, the Champlain Canal and the Hud
 son River. A longtime builder\, designer and cabinetmaker\, Clark draws on
  decades of exploring the region’s waterways and landscapes to bring an 
 authentic sense of place to his fiction. Bear Pond Books Stowe Bear Pond B
 ooks Stowe 38 Main St Stowe \, Vermont 05672 (802) 253-8236 https://stoweb
