BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Folk Show's Annual Potluck Dinner
DTSTART:20261121T140000
DTEND:20261121T170000
DTSTAMP:20261120T190958Z
UID:9f9bc4a01bc5571a1ff6d62475e7d9@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:To bring our New Hampshire and Vermont folk music communities 
 together this year\, NHPR's Kate McNally is hosting our annual potluck and
  live music gathering right on the NH/VT line in Norwich\, Vermont. Save y
 ourself a seat! Whether you're making the trip from across the Connecticut
  River or just down the road\, come share a dish\, play a song\, or simply
  enjoy a cozy afternoon with fellow public radio folk fans. Event Details 
 Date: Saturday\, Nov. 21 Time: 2 p.m. to 5 p.m. (Doors open at 2 PM\; plea
 se arrive by 2:45 p.m.) Location: Unitarian Universalist Congregation of t
 he Upper Valley\, Norwich\, Vermont Bring your favorite savory dish\, appe
 tizer\, or dessert! To help us coordinate the cross-border feast\, please 
 send a quick email to folkshow@nhpr.org letting us know what you plan to b
 ring. Acoustic instruments & songs: Starting at 3 p.m.\, Kate will host a 
 rotating open mic. Pack your acoustic instrument and a couple of songs\, o
 r just grab a plate and enjoy the music. Come hungry\, bring your good vib
 es\, and let’s celebrate our shared love for great folk music together. 
 Unitarian Universalist Congregation of the Upper Valley\n\nSources: Vermon
 t Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
